# Build context for both infra/Dockerfile.api and infra/Dockerfile.web is the repository
# root. Without this file the daemon would ship node_modules, every bin/obj tree and the
# whole .git history to the builder on every build.
#
# Note the deliberate absence of a blanket `*` allowlist pattern: the two images need
# different subtrees (backend/ and frontend/ + infra/), so this is a denylist.

# Version control and CI
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Secrets and local environment
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.pfx
**/*.p12

# .NET build output. Copying a host bin/obj into the image poisons the build with
# artefacts compiled against a different SDK and defeats layer caching.
**/bin
**/obj
**/artifacts
**/TestResults
**/*.user
**/*.suo
**/.vs

# Node
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.angular
**/npm-debug.log*
**/coverage
**/.eslintcache

# Documentation and infrastructure that no image needs. infra/ itself is NOT excluded:
# Dockerfile.web copies infra/nginx.conf and infra/web-entrypoint.sh from the context.
docs
LICENSE
**/*.md

# IDE and OS
.idea
**/.vscode
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/*.swp
